# Task Planner — cloud configuration and local data (added in Stage 13)
#
# `gradle.properties` is deliberately NOT ignored: it is committed and carries build switches. That is exactly
# why the four Firebase values must never go there — see firebase.example.properties for where they belong.
firebase.properties
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
# A safety snapshot is the reader's database, copied. It lives in app-private storage on a device, and this
# line is the guard against a debugging run ever dropping one next to the sources.
safety/

# Stage 15 privacy: the user's real Google Keep text export and the derived backups of it are personal
# data. They are measured locally and never committed; CI runs against the depersonalized fixture under
# app/src/test/resources/keep/, which reproduces the same structure with neutral titles.
google-keep-original-export.txt
Вставленный текст*.txt
task_planner_google_keep_import.json
taskplanner-backup-google-keep*.json
